15 - 7 + 5 = 13. She started with 15 stickers, lost 7, so she had 15 - 7 = 8 stickers. Then she received 5 more, so she had 8 + 5 = 13 stickers.
The problem states that Jasmine received 15 stickers initially. She lost 7, so we subtract 7 from 15: 15 - 7 = 8. Then, she received 5 more stickers, so we add 5 to 8: 8 + 5 = 13. Therefore, Jasmine has 13 stickers at the end.

